From 6f701c8bf86d2c722602011c07ff49e093f82dfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Solomon <solomon@regentplatform.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 10:11:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add item-linked sales with discounts, custody eligibility
 flags, inventory analytics
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three related gaps in the inventory module:

1. Quick Sales had no link to stock — a sale never decremented
   inventory, and there was no way to record the actual price charged
   vs list price (e.g. a discount).
2. Custody showed every item in the org, including pure-retail stock
   that should never be issued to staff.
3. No inventory-level analytics: value on hand, units/revenue sold
   over time, category breakdown.

Schema (20260824000001_item_sales_and_custody_flags.sql):
- items gains can_sell / can_custody booleans (default true/false so
  nothing existing changes behavior; items already carrying custody
  metadata are backfilled to can_custody = true so live assignments
  don't disappear).
- daily_sales gains item_id, quantity, unit_list_price,
  unit_sale_price, discount_amount, discount_pct, item_movement_id.
- create_item_sale_v1: sells a specific item/quantity/price, decrements
  stock and records the item_movement inline (NOT via
  update_item_quantity_v1, whose role gate excludes 'staff' — inlining
  matches the existing create_daily_sale_v1/create_expense_v1 pattern
  and its documented reason), computes discount_amount/pct from list
  vs charged price, and posts the same balanced journal entry the
  free-text flow already does. Row is locked FOR UPDATE to avoid a
  lost update on concurrent sales of the same item.

Frontend:
- QuickSaleForm: tabbed into 'Sell an item' (picks stock, defaults
  price to list price, shows live discount) and 'Other sale' (the
  original free-text flow, unchanged).
- ItemForm: two checkboxes (Sellable / Custody-eligible), item must
  be at least one.
- CustodyView: filters to can_custody items only instead of listing
  every item in the org.
- InventoryAnalytics: value at cost/selling price, units sold and
  real revenue (from daily_sales.amount, not list-price approximation)
  over a selectable timeframe, total discounts given, units-sold bar
  chart, stock-value-by-category pie chart. Mounted on both the
  Inventory page and the main Dashboard per request.

Typecheck and lint clean across the repo. Migration not yet applied
against a live database — review before running.
